<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia wages rise 11.5 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Malaysia wages rise 11.5 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian wages increased by 11.5 percent in 1996 against a rise of 19.3 percent in 1995, the central bank, Bank Negara, said in its 1996 annual report published on Friday.</p>
<p>The unusually high rise in 1995 was due to a &quot;significantly higher wage increase in the agriculture sector,&quot; it said</p>
<p>&quot;Wage increases (in 1996) were most significant for the manufacturing sector, rising by 15 percent, and in the services sector where wages were 10.1 percent higher,&quot; said Bank Negara.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603 201 4813)</p>
</text>
